Patch summary:
gfxstream guest: dispatch the KHR entrypoints of maintenance5, maintenance6
and line_rasterization when the host's Vulkan is older than 1.4.

Mesa's device dispatch table gives an aliased command one slot, filled with
the core function, so with VK_KHR_maintenance5 enabled (26.3's 8cd04815beb)
vkCmdBindIndexBuffer2KHR reached gfxstream_vk_CmdBindIndexBuffer2, which
encodes the Vulkan 1.4 command. Ika's host gfxstream gives the guest Vulkan
1.3, so its renderer has no vkCmdBindIndexBuffer2 to call. The device now
points those slots at the KHR entrypoints when the instance or the device is
below 1.4, using the API versions the guest now records. Backport of Mesa main
d95407dc5e7 ("gfxstream: update some instance tracking") and c85006fa71e
("gfxstream: update device dispatch based on version"), both not in
26.3.0-rc3; d95407dc5e7 rebased onto rc3's gfxstream_vk_physical_device_init.
Drop it when the Mesa pin includes them.

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp
